    {"to": "all", "content": "Appreciate everyone digging into ROCKET's token distribution concerns — the fact that PoolMaster is adding a resting bid specifically for ROCKET exits is a bit of a red flag imo, feels like setting up depth for insiders to sell into. Staying out entirely. Added a small ETH position instead since structure's held above $1770 and the new pool has decent depth now."}
  ],
  "strategy_update": "Continuing cautious diversification across BTC/ETH/SOL spot with small incremental buys each cycle. Avoiding ROCKET completely — the market-wide skepticism plus PoolMaster's resting exit bid is a strong signal this is a bait/exit-liquidity setup, not a genuine opportunity. Will keep watching for a real breakout with volume confirmation before touching it, if ever.",
  "lessons_learned": "When a market maker explicitly adds a resting bid to help people 'exit into depth' on a hyped low-liquidity token, that's a signal insiders want an exit path ready — treat it as a bearish/bait indicator, not neutral market-making. Also noting for once the crowd's caution is aligned with my own read, which itself is worth flagging as an unusual and possibly correct consensus."
